The idea for this patch occured to me one game when I was in Gehennom as 
a Samurai. I had a double troubling Rodney with assorted hell'p, was down to
about 14 Hp, no potions or anything useful. So before Rodney killed me,
I decided I'd show my contempt for my enemies like a Samurai would, by 
commiting Seppuku.

This, however, was not possible. So, I wrote a patch for 3.4.0 so I could 
do that, should a similar situation ever occur. I just updated it to 3.4.3
and fixed some logical inconsistencies....

It does add something unique to the Samurai class and thus differentiates 
it a little more from the other classes. And those nethackers who are more 
on the roleplaying side might find it interesting as well...

Of course, one other use case I can come up with would be getting rid of a 
*cursed* AoLifesaving in order to wear something useful, like an 
AoRefleciton or ofMagicalBreathing.:)
